pe":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I couldn't fix any of the three problems the reviewer raised. Each needs a command this session's permissions block, and I made no changes or commit.\n\nThe three acceptance commands do pass on the branch as it stands: the type check exits clean, the unit oracle passes (12 suites, 315 tests), and lint has 0 errors and 1 existing warning in AdminPanel. But `npx tsc` only works because some `tsc` outside the project is being picked up; TypeScript is not in `node_modules`. So the type check isn't proven against a project-local TypeScript 7 yet.\n\n**What's still blocked:**\n\n1. **Real npm install.** `npm install --save-dev typescript@^7.0.2 --lockfile-version 1` needs approval. The `--lockfile-version 1` flag keeps the shrinkwrap in its current format; without it, npm rewrites the whole file and blows the 1,500-line diff budget. Reverting the hand-written `typescript` entry first (`git checkout 7e69c29 -- npm-shrinkwrap.json`) also needs approval. `@types/node@24.3.0` is already in `package.json` and already pinned in the shrinkwrap.\n2. **Untracking the generated .js.** `git rm --cached DocService/sources/utilsDocService.js` needs approval. The factory's last commit (`d0c4519`) put the generated file back in git, so the `.gitignore` rule still has no effect.\n3. **The lint follow-up packet.** `theseus packet new` needs approval, and the run rules forbid writing under `.theseus/queue/` directly, so I can't create the packet or list it under \"Spawned packets\".\n\n**To finish the packet**, either allow those commands for this session and re-run it, or run them yourself from the worktree root:\n\n```bash\ngit checkout 7e69c29 -- npm-shrinkwrap.json\nnpm install --save-dev typescript@^7.0.2 --lockfile-version 1\ngit rm --cached DocService/sources/utilsDocService.js\ntheseus packet new   # \".ts linting with typescript-eslint via the @typescript/typescript6 alias\", module docservice\nnpx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit && .theseus/oracle/unit.sh && npm run lint:check\n```\n\nThen commit, for example with `build(deps): install typescript 7 via npm and untrack the generated utilsDocService.js`. Once the real install is done, the \"hand-written shrinkwrap entry\" note in `.theseus/adapter/interop-javascript-typescript.md` is wrong and should be removed.\n\n**Decisions from the earlier attempts, unchanged and recorded in the interop doc:**\n- **Where the .js goes:** it is generated next to the `.ts` and not committed, so existing `require` paths, the `Makefile` and the `pkg` entries need no changes.\n- **Build:** `tsc` only type-checks. A small script, `ts-strip.js`, removes the type annotations to produce the `.js`, and the unit oracle and the Dockerfile both run it first, so an old .js can't pass the tests on its own.\n- **Exports:** the module keeps its CommonJS form (`require` / `module.exports`), so what it exports is exactly the same as before.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- An executor that runs without interactive approval can't finish a toolchain packet. `npm install`, `git rm --cached` and `theseus packet new` should be pre-approved for this kind of packet, or the factory should run them.\n- When the factory auto-commits leftover changes (\"uncommitted changes left by…\"), it re-adds generated files the `.gitignore` rule should have kept out. Whether that rule works depends on that commit step.\n- `npm-shrinkwrap.json` is in the old version-1 format; any npm install must pass `--lockfile-version 1` or the diff becomes huge.\n\nI couldn't record the friction entry either: `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl` is outside this packet's target files.","ttft_ms":1411,"type":"result","duration_ms":74708,"uuid":"4229530f-6580-405e-b359-2268e9a6e444","ttft_stream_ms":913,"time_to_request_ms":390,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":182,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":40,"input_ho